 play differently  the style this year  with golden state i think it's too  ingrained i don't think anything can  change from a system standpoint and then  certainly  nobody's filling clay's role he did so  many things for them  and we we know about the jumpers but  defensively  steve kerr loved the fact that you could  just throw him out there on the floor  and he would take care of whoever the  best  wing defender was on the other team so  he trusted him  immensely but i'd say on top of  who fills the wing rolls and that's  where the warriors were short already  it was kind of only clay and andrew  wiggins the  the part that's really hurting  internally right now  is the emotional side because this is a  guy  even with steph and draymond and kd when  he was there  clay was the most beloved clay was the  guy that  really set the tone behind the scenes  and and curtis talked about it a lot  over the years clay is an egoless player  he can just kind of fit in  and do whatever they needed and to see  that he may be  down again for a while is really hurting  everybody on that team right now yeah  i remember steve kerr telling me years  ago he just said clay  is uh there's no maintenance to it like  i don't have to worry about  anything it's not touches or being a  star  or points or anything he said he just he  is maintenance free  and that's rare it's very rare and he  doesn't want any part of the spotlight  and then in all the years i've covered  the league i i certainly have never  seen anybody like clay because he he  goes and hits all these shots and  is a really solid defender when he wants  to be and then he just kind of goes home  and he's content just kind of hanging  out with his dog and doing his own thing  he doesn't like talking to the media  although he's one of the best quotes on  the team and  that resonates for a lot of people and  it's not to say that  they don't love steph and draymond in  their own way because they absolutely do  it's just that clay marches to his own  beat and it's  so different than most stars in the  league and that's what made him unique  so on top of the fact that  consistently he was out there game after  game  putting in the work and putting up the  numbers  it was the tone he set with all the  other star power on that roster that  that kerr and myers love so much you  have an owner who  seems like he's pretty aggressive to get  fans in the stands this upcoming season  what is the game plan he's going to try  the lake of his as much as he can to get  people in there  then the reality though is it's going to  be tough because san francisco is  is starting to shut uh more again  after a recent surge in inktober cases  so  lacup is still gonna to push the  envelope the warriors are behind him  he's gonna put his  own money in to do it it's just gonna be  so difficult and and i can just tell you  personally i i was living 10 minutes  away from the arena  to see that thing empty day after day  is is a crusher uh for for that team  and for ownership because that was  supposed to be the cash towel of cash  cows  and it's not to say it still can't be  over time  but it's empty it was supposed to be  filled  every day with concerts and other events  all the time on top of all the games and  and now  to see that the way it is that's why  you're seeing from wake up and from the  warriors this push so hard to get  some people back in there and start to  get the revenue streams going again  is there a time frame for this mri today  with klay thompson  i would expect the news in the next  couple hours i i  i think everybody was expecting it to be  in the morning and you mentioned kerr  and some of the trainers are headed down  there and  it may be there in the moment but i  would expect  something here very soon nick thanks for  joining us we appreciate your time  dan i've listened to you my whole life i  i really appreciate you guys having me  thank you nick that's uh nick friedel he  covers the warriors for espn.com

